WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.802
-our next guest is an
Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.170
you know from his work
in "The Crown," "Downton Abbey"

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.606
and "The Imitation Game."

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:10.075
He stars as Hollywood icon
Robert Evans in "The Offers" --

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:11.644
"The Offer" -- Excuse me.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.946
You can watch the finale
this Thursday,

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:16.649
streaming on Paramount+.
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.418
-Can I get a vodka martini with
a wisp of vermouth and a twist?

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.921
Two?
-Uh, it's 11:00 a.m.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.923
-One.
-Yes, sir.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:27.827
-Everything okay in your world?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.029
Why wouldn't it be?
Robert. Robert, Robert.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.931
I loved the script, man.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.766
I love the twists.
I love the tone.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.901
You've really elevated
the idea of a P.I.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.170
-Thanks.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.339
-If there's one thing --
just one small thing --

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.808
the conspiracy
is a little hard to follow.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:46.345
So if you had to, just for me,
if you had to,

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.714
talk about "Chinatown,"
the themes, et cetera,

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:51.317
what would the pitch be, man?

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.687
-Please welcome to the show
Matthew Goode, everybody!

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.089
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.358
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:06.932
♪♪

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.801
Thank you for being here!

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.970
-Thank you very much.
My pleasure.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.905
-This is -- This is
such a wonderful show.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.940
This is a mini series --
a 10-episode miniseries

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.542
about the making
of "The Godfather"

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.811
and all the incredible hurdles
that had to be overcome.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:22.081
Do you remember the first time
you saw "The Godfather"?

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.382
'Cause I know I certainly do.

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.485
-It was just before
I went to drama school,

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.753
and I thought I should
probably watch something

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.856
that, you know,
might make me a better actor.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.192
And, yeah -- and it was --
I was legal.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.426
It was one of the first times
I was legal

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.128
to actually watch an 18 video.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:37.697
-Which shows
how long ago that was.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.398
-Were they pretty --
Growing up in England,

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.568
were they pretty strict
about that, getting --

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.235
-No, not in my local shop
in my village.

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:44.470
I grew up in the countryside,
so it'd be like

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.105
you put bubble gum
on the counter,

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.340
barely had your head above it,
and then it'd be like

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.176
"RoboCop" would go down.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.378
Just cross your fingers
and hope you got it.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.781
-You play Robert Evans,
who's an icon,

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:58.951
and it's such a rich,
I would imagine, fun character

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.186
to play.
-I mean...

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.620
-Not even -- He is
both a character,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.922
but obviously
he's a real person.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.357
-Yeah, he's a real person.
But, no, yeah,

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.125
it was quite daunting actually,
if anything,

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:09.929
because he has such
an extraordinary cadence

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.164
and, you know,
and timbre to his voice.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:15.201
So I spent a lot of time
watching videos on YouTube --

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.369
like, old sort of things he did.
So, yeah.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.504
-Just old interviews.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:19.705
And "The Kid Stays
in the Picture,"

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.140
I imagine that was a helpful...

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.277
-Oh, that's one of the best,
you know, documentaries ever.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.345
But, no, because actually I
didn't listen to that too much,

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.814
because he's like 70 then,
and the rhythm has changed.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.817
-Oh, right, you had to get
the right -- right era voice.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.451
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But there's loads of wormholes

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:34.253
on YouTube you can go down.
It's phenomenal.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:36.356
-And you were -- You had time
for wormholes,

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.190
because you were basically,
because of COVID,

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.660
just stuck in a hotel room.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.695
I mean, it was --
Because if you get COVID,

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.997
then they, you know,
they shut the production down

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:46.499
and then it costs
a lot of money,

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.467
so I was terrified.
So if I wasn't filming,

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.537
I'd be in the -- just in
the hotel room, doing homework.

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:53.873
It was quite boring.
I lived like a monk.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.242
-Is it true --
because I feel like

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.744
this happens very rarely
for my British friends.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.446
But you actually were stuck
in a hotel long enough

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.482
that you actually started liking
American football?

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:06.019
-Yeah. No, that's --
That's actually not even a joke.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.388
What a great season it was.
-Yeah, right?

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:10.990
Thank you. There you go.
[ Applause ]

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.758
All it takes --
-Yeah.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.628
-All it takes is
a pandemic and a lockdown.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.863
-But it was like --
But also Sunday's a long day

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.132
if you're in that room
on your own,

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.100
so you're like, "Three games
I'm gonna watch."

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.669
So that's like
nine hours of fun.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:26.038
And the best game was
Bills against the Chiefs.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.240
-Yeah, one of the greatest games
of all time.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.743
Now you're -- The only thing
I have to say is, I'm so sorry,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.777
they don't always go like that.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.446
Yeah, they're not all...

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.713
-I'll take it. I don't mind.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:37.516
-I want to ask
about the wardrobe,

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:39.652
because this is I think,
a very, again,

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.820
iconic era of Hollywood --
'60s, '70s.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.323
-Yeah.
-Robert Evans obviously

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.659
had a sartorial style
all of his own.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.661
Did you enjoy wearing
his clothes?

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.463
-Well, yeah.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.632
I mean, there were some
pretty strong looks there.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.500
-Yeah.
-I don't love polyester...

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.868
-Yeah.
-...that much,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.236
and so there is an element
of like, "Well,

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.640
it looks great,"
but you're sort of on set

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.241
and just itchy.
But it was, you know,

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.409
anything for the craft, darling.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.409 --> 00:04:06.946
-We so appreciate
your sacrifice.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:10.216
-But also I got -- you know,
because Robert had these --

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:13.486
Really what's iconic with him is
his enormous lenses

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.821
that he wore on his face.
So they brought out --

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.790
I had like 25 pairs,
and they were like,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.158
"Which one do you think
you'll wear?"

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.428
I think, "The lot.
Let's wear all of them."

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.798
-You did a wine show

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.833
with our friend Matthew Rhys,
and your friend Matthew Rhys.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.469
-Which is I was nearly here
with the...

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.137
-Yeah, the two of you were
supposed to come here together.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.772
-Yeah, I think one of
our children's birthdays

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:36.141
got in the way.
-We celebrate

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:38.177
your being a better father
than talk-show host.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.945
Talk-show guest, I should say.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.580
I would be here no matter what.
-It was a great show, though.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.317
-Oh, thank you. Yeah, well --
But you -- I want to ask,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.219
because I've done some
day drinking on this show.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:49.021
-I saw your one with Lorde.
It was great.

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:51.257
-But there, it takes you
out of you.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.525
A long day of wine drinking,
isn't that...

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.761
How was recovery?
You did 10 episodes.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.429
-Well, it was --
I mean, we were doing, I think,

00:04:57.429 --> 00:05:00.099
40 wines in a day.
And you know, and Matthew and I

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.201
sort of -- we went hard,
at the beginning.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.070
And then you get -- You know,
like five hours into filming,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.773
the director will be like,
"Can we go again, guys?

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:09.875
This is a joke."
And you'd be like, "What?"

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.044
And he goes, "The word
[Slurring] 'decision'

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:13.913
[Normal voice]
didn't come out very well."

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.582
So, yeah.
You must find that, too, right?

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.217
-Yes, but we only --
it's only two hours.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.586
It's smash-and-grab for us.
We're, like, in and out.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.355
And nobody's watching it
to learn anything about wine.

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:26.192
-We don't learn anything.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.760
-No, that comes across.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.562
-We're just idiots, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.696
-I have to ask this, though.

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:34.033
You didn't meet Matthew
on that show?

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.836
-No, I've known about him
for years,

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:40.373
and we used to meet each other
in, like, costume fittings,

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.441
and he'd be getting his trousers
off over that,

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.810
and me being like...
And so I'd speak to him

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.278
through a curtain,
and then we met on this.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:47.879
-This is -- I wanted to
show this

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:51.918
because this, to me, is
the most British title of a show

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.653
that I think I've ever seen.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.556
And look, everything about
"Death Comes to Pemberley."

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.023
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.023 --> 00:06:00.392
-It's an instant classic.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:02.862
-I feel like definitely --
you're definitely

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.463
wearing an outfit
that I'm super psyched

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:05.831
is in
"Death Comes to Pemberley."

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.400
And...
-Matthew looks like

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.102
he's about to murder someone.
-Yeah.

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:10.869
That's not
the free-wheeling Matthew.

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:12.905
This is after they told him
there's no more wine.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.207
-Oh, I love it.
I mean, he is the nicest,

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.476
funniest person
you'll ever meet.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:19.044
-To watch him seem dour
is a very not --

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:20.545
out of character
with the real man.

00:06:20.545 --> 00:06:21.814
-Yeah.
-Hey, thank you so much

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.349
for being here.
Congrats on the show.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.184
You are really
a fantastic Robert Evans.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.952
-Thank you very much, Seth.
-Thank you.

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.287
Matthew Goode, everybody.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.122
"The Offer,"
streaming on Paramount+.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:32.392
We'll be right back with
a performance from Jewel.

